# Copyable chat output

Cursor shows a copy control on fenced code blocks, not on ordinary prose. There is no separate copy-icon API.

When the reply contains anything Joel may need to copy — paste-ready Cursor prompts, `prompt?` replies, emails, commands, paths, HEAD SHAs, Alembic revisions, report field blocks — put that content in a fenced code block.

**Put the primary copyable fence last among copyable blocks.** Brief context may go above. Do not put explanation, options, or follow-up questions after the fence, except the required CalibAi `END — <title>` line below.

If several things are copyable, the fence Joel is meant to copy now (usually the full prompt) is the last **copyable** block in the reply.

Do this even when the same facts also appear in prose. Do not leave copyable commands or prompt text in prose only.

**CalibAi chat-title continuity:** After that primary fence, the only permitted trailing line is:

`END — <exact active ChatGPT development chat title>`

Do not put explanation, options, or follow-up questions after that END line. Canonical: `docs/governance/continuity-and-anti-drift.md`.

Keep secrets, passwords, and SECRET_KEY values out of chat, fenced or not.
